update your stock ledger to reflect the reverse split.

.why = your internal records must match the filed Certificate of Amendment.

---

## stock ledger update

| field | before | after |
|-------|--------|-------|
| shareholder | | (same) |
| shares held | | (÷ ratio) |
| par value | $ | $ (× ratio) |
| total value | $ | $ (same) |

---

## cap table (if applicable)

if you use Carta, Pulley, or similar:
1. record the reverse split transaction
2. verify share counts match

if spreadsheet:
1. update share counts
2. update par value
3. add note with effective date and ratio

---

## stock certificates (if issued)

if you issued paper certificates:
1. cancel old certificates
2. issue new certificates with updated share count
3. note: most startups don't issue paper certificates

---

## emit

save updated ledger to:
`$route/4.update.ledger.yield.md`
